WEBVTT

00:00.530 --> 00:02.150
Is that... Challe?

00:03.490 --> 00:04.440
What?

00:04.750 --> 00:06.400
Miss Bridget?

00:10.360 --> 00:12.360
But the other day, when I saw you...

00:12.770 --> 00:15.360
my heart raced so fast 
I didn't know what to do.

00:31.480 --> 00:39.500
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but…</i>

00:46.190 --> 00:48.920
<i>It's all right</i>

00:48.920 --> 00:52.760
<i>Even alone, I'll be fine, but…</i>

00:52.760 --> 00:59.260
<i>You know, the truth is
 that no one is alone</i>

00:59.260 --> 01:05.830
<i>Things like happiness, 
loneliness, and even anxiety…</i>

01:05.830 --> 01:15.160
<i>We are born to savor all those things</i>

01:15.590 --> 01:18.800
<i>A single spoonful of sparkles</i>

01:18.800 --> 01:21.930
<i>Transforms everything into smiles</i>

01:22.220 --> 01:29.050
<i>That could be what I secretly wished for…</i>

01:29.050 --> 01:31.730
<i>That miracle</i>

01:31.980 --> 01:38.700
<i>We're each searching for
 our most precious treasures</i>

01:38.700 --> 01:45.000
<i>That's what our journey is for</i>

01:45.000 --> 01:52.130
<i>I don't know how far I can go, but...</i>

01:52.130 --> 02:00.360
<i>Each moment that passes before me
 shall be spun from hope</i>

02:03.680 --> 02:06.260
So, what is this thing 
you wanted my advice about?

02:06.750 --> 02:09.740
I never said anything 
about wanting advice, did I?

02:09.740 --> 02:12.300
I only asked if you might want to take a walk.

02:12.300 --> 02:13.880
Don't play innocent.

02:13.880 --> 02:16.140
It's Challe, right? Something about him?

02:16.140 --> 02:18.120
Did something nice happen recently?

02:21.220 --> 02:22.620
Nothing, huh?

02:23.330 --> 02:25.180
Well, for the past week...

02:25.180 --> 02:29.080
he's spent every night 
modeling like that for Kieth.

02:32.840 --> 02:35.130
What are you doing?

02:35.420 --> 02:37.240
My, how carefree you seem!

02:37.240 --> 02:39.800
Master Jonas is going to go work on his piece.

02:39.800 --> 02:40.910
And you?

02:40.910 --> 02:42.090
Have you finished already?

02:42.740 --> 02:44.960
Or, could it be that you've given u—

02:44.960 --> 02:47.060
That's enough. Be quiet, Cathy.

02:47.660 --> 02:50.660
This year, I'm going to make a proper piece...

02:51.080 --> 02:53.400
a piece that I want to create.

02:54.190 --> 02:56.670
I know you'll probably make something, too.

02:56.670 --> 02:58.890
And your expression says 
I'm not worth worrying about.

03:00.040 --> 03:00.860
Jonas?

03:02.050 --> 03:05.450
I'm sure of it now. I hate you.

03:06.640 --> 03:09.560
"A piece that I want to create"?

03:13.860 --> 03:16.120
Looks like they're done for today.

03:16.120 --> 03:17.210
Yes.

03:19.080 --> 03:23.020
May I ask? Why did you want to 
have Challe as your model?

03:23.420 --> 03:24.680
Well...

03:25.200 --> 03:30.940
because the royal family tends to 
favor sugar confections with a fairy motif.

03:32.270 --> 03:35.980
If you visit the head temple of the kingdom's 
religion, the Church of Saint Lewiston Bell,

03:35.980 --> 03:38.700
there's a book about the royal 
family and sugar confections.

03:42.000 --> 03:45.660
I wonder why the royal family 
favors sugar confections of fairies.

03:46.790 --> 03:48.450
The Church of Saint Lewiston Bell?

03:48.720 --> 03:49.900
Why would you do that?

03:49.900 --> 03:52.200
Tomorrow's a rare day off, you know?

03:52.200 --> 03:54.440
There's something I want to look into.

03:54.440 --> 03:59.370
It might be something I need to 
create a piece for the Exhibition.

03:59.370 --> 04:01.050
I was wondering if you might come with me.

04:02.950 --> 04:04.220
Do as you like.

04:22.070 --> 04:24.890
I'm sorry for making you come with me.

04:24.890 --> 04:26.760
You're being strangely meek.

04:26.760 --> 04:28.700
It isn't like you, Scarecrow.

04:29.270 --> 04:33.460
I'm not, really. I just thought 
you might have plans, Challe.

04:34.260 --> 04:36.420
A date with Miss Bridget or something.

04:36.910 --> 04:39.690
Bridget? Who is that?

04:39.690 --> 04:41.180
Please don't pretend you don't know.

04:41.180 --> 04:45.050
Yesterday afternoon, you two 
embraced behind the dormitory.

04:45.050 --> 04:47.270
I saw you.

04:49.150 --> 04:52.340
So, Bridget would be that woman's name, then.

04:52.840 --> 04:55.850
Challe! You didn't know 
her name, and you still...

04:56.440 --> 05:00.280
She kept chattering on about 
whether she'd buy me or not,

05:00.280 --> 05:02.790
so I told her that if she wanted me, 
she should steal my wing.

05:03.480 --> 05:06.320
There have always been humans like that.

05:07.380 --> 05:09.780
I-Is that what that was...

05:10.790 --> 05:15.290
Then that was the reason you've 
seemed out of sorts since yesterday?

05:16.040 --> 05:18.330
If I had to pick a reason, it would be you.

05:19.080 --> 05:19.770
What?

05:25.720 --> 05:28.220
I'm sorry, but you won't 
be able to enter the library.

05:28.710 --> 05:30.720
It's under renovation at the moment, you see.

05:30.720 --> 05:33.180
Though... Now, what was it again?

05:33.710 --> 05:36.170
Books about the royal family 
and sugar confections.

05:37.060 --> 05:39.340
We do have such things,

05:39.340 --> 05:43.210
but the older books are all 
written in old Highlandian script.

05:43.210 --> 05:45.000
You won't be able to read them.

05:46.240 --> 05:49.410
Is that ancient Highlandian script?

05:53.390 --> 05:56.470
The battle between our founding king, 
Cedric, and the Fairy King.

05:57.260 --> 06:01.020
Now that I think of it, 
I don't know the Fairy King's name.

06:01.650 --> 06:03.340
Riselva Cyril Sash.

06:04.520 --> 06:06.590
How do you know that?

06:06.590 --> 06:08.780
I've known it since I was born.

06:08.780 --> 06:12.390
It's likely that 
the obsidian I was born from knew.

06:12.890 --> 06:15.520
I will tell you what is written there.

06:15.520 --> 06:18.060
You can read it? The old Highlandian script?

06:18.740 --> 06:20.020
It seems so.

06:21.460 --> 06:25.480
King Cedric was the Fairy King's slave.

06:25.770 --> 06:27.070
Slave?!

06:27.450 --> 06:31.660
But the Fairy King, because of 
Cedric's bravery and sincerity,

06:31.660 --> 06:34.030
regarded him as a friend and set him free.

06:34.560 --> 06:36.210
And Cedric...

06:36.210 --> 06:39.560
he respected the Fairy King 
for his integrity and strength,

06:40.000 --> 06:41.430
and considered him a friend.

06:44.390 --> 06:48.510
Friends? The Fairy King and King Cedric?

06:48.510 --> 06:53.480
The two kings searched for a path that 
fairies and humans could walk together.

06:54.480 --> 06:56.590
But while the humans revered King Cedric,

06:56.590 --> 06:59.600
and the fairies felt 
the same for the Fairy King,

06:59.600 --> 07:00.690
they hated each other.

07:01.220 --> 07:03.000
War broke out.

07:03.000 --> 07:04.490
Destiny became twisted.

07:05.480 --> 07:08.870
The Fairy King was defeated and Cedric won.

07:09.340 --> 07:12.030
Cedric grieved the death of 
his friend very deeply.

07:12.430 --> 07:16.490
In memoriam, he had a sugar 
confection made in his friend's image,

07:16.490 --> 07:18.070
and offered up a prayer.

07:18.650 --> 07:22.960
He wished that the world they'd 
dreamed of would one day come to pass.

07:23.800 --> 07:28.650
A power which brought great good fortune 
came to dwell within that sugar confection.

07:32.230 --> 07:33.920
That's all of it.

07:33.920 --> 07:38.080
God wanted humans 
to become rulers over the earth,

07:38.080 --> 07:42.910
but the human woman fell in love with 
the Fairy King and pledged her loyalty to him.

07:42.910 --> 07:47.470
The one who cleansed that sin and 
created the world that God wished for...

07:47.470 --> 07:49.290
was King Cedric.

07:49.730 --> 07:51.100
It's completely different.

07:51.100 --> 07:54.860
Different from what we humans... 
from the teachings of the kingdom's religion.

07:54.860 --> 07:57.310
Something that's rewritten 
for convenience's sake...

07:57.310 --> 07:58.540
That's "history," isn't it?

07:59.540 --> 08:00.650
It's so underhanded.

08:02.210 --> 08:06.380
But why would Ancestor King Cedric 
create a world like this?

08:06.380 --> 08:09.710
A world where humans make fairies serve them?

08:09.710 --> 08:12.040
He wanted us to live side-by-side.

08:12.040 --> 08:15.100
He didn't create it. 
He wasn't able to create that world.

08:16.620 --> 08:19.260
Cedric had won the war.

08:19.260 --> 08:22.330
He may still have wanted to search for 
a path toward coexistence.

08:23.090 --> 08:27.120
But he wasn't able to create that world, 
so the world became as it is now.

08:27.120 --> 08:28.920
That's all it is.

08:31.540 --> 08:33.950
The difference between races... is vast.

08:34.370 --> 08:36.380
Please, don't say such things.

08:36.380 --> 08:37.940
There isn't any difference.

08:38.530 --> 08:39.380
There is.

08:41.510 --> 08:42.620
There isn't.

08:42.620 --> 08:44.270
For me, there isn't any difference.

08:44.270 --> 08:48.040
After all, Challe, I feel so much...

08:58.200 --> 09:01.490
The reasons the royal family 
favors fairy sugar confections...

09:01.490 --> 09:03.280
are Cedric's regrets...

09:03.280 --> 09:07.520
and atonement for not being able to 
carry on his will. Perhaps that's it.

09:07.900 --> 09:08.730
Challe!

09:26.560 --> 09:28.010
I found it.

09:31.030 --> 09:33.090
I'll make it.

09:33.630 --> 09:36.840
There's something I want to create!

09:41.840 --> 09:43.930
So, how'd things turn out?

09:44.300 --> 09:45.720
Wonderfully.

09:45.720 --> 09:47.890
I found the motif for my piece.

09:48.360 --> 09:50.640
I'm going to make my sugar confection now.

09:50.640 --> 09:53.600
Will you help me, Mithril Lid Pod?

09:53.600 --> 09:55.990
Y-Yeah. Leave it to me!

10:00.500 --> 10:01.420
Challe.

10:03.350 --> 10:06.910
If you aren't against the idea, 
I'd like you to stay, too.

10:08.420 --> 10:09.910
You won't be distracted?

10:14.980 --> 10:16.200
I want you here.

10:33.520 --> 10:34.870
<i>I want to give it form...</i>

10:35.490 --> 10:38.030
<i>that which our founding king 
and the Fairy King held within them...</i>

10:39.350 --> 10:41.130
<i>the wish they shared!</i>

10:45.260 --> 10:46.080
I see!

10:46.590 --> 10:48.920
Anne is beginning her creation at last!

10:48.920 --> 10:51.250
I'm so glad. I was worried.

10:51.900 --> 10:53.050
Worried?

10:53.050 --> 10:55.670
Because it seemed like she 
was troubled by something.

10:56.090 --> 10:58.060
"The truth is, you don't have time for this."

10:58.060 --> 11:01.080
"For you, everything is riding on this year."

11:01.080 --> 11:02.700
The words came right up to here.

11:03.160 --> 11:06.220
But then it wouldn't be a fair fight anymore.

11:10.730 --> 11:13.130
She was troubled by something?

11:13.130 --> 11:14.120
What is this?

11:14.120 --> 11:16.000
"You can't" and "it's impossible"!

11:16.000 --> 11:17.360
That's all anyone ever says!

11:17.360 --> 11:20.300
Well, the impossible is impossible, right?

11:20.300 --> 11:23.870
But that Anne girl has been recognized 
as a legitimate artisan!

11:22.160 --> 11:23.710
I wish they'd pipe down.

11:23.710 --> 11:25.680
At this rate, I won't be able to sleep.

11:23.870 --> 11:25.710
What? Why are you bringing that up now?

11:25.680 --> 11:27.390
Oh. Challe, you're here?

11:25.710 --> 11:27.880
We're talking about that fairy, aren't we?

11:27.390 --> 11:29.620
Is she having a bout of, 
what's it called... hysteria?

11:27.880 --> 11:30.200
I don't want to be fettered 
any more than I already am!

11:29.940 --> 11:32.840
That girl seems to be 
pretty obsessed with you.

11:30.200 --> 11:32.380
I don't want to give up 
on what I want anymore!

11:32.380 --> 11:35.720
Please, Bridget, won't you calm down a little?

11:32.840 --> 11:35.080
She's been begging Elliott to buy you for her.

11:35.080 --> 11:36.640
And when she realized that wasn't possible,

11:36.640 --> 11:39.630
she wanted him to get someone 
to steal your wing.

11:39.630 --> 11:40.790
You'd better be careful.

11:41.200 --> 11:43.230
I am not that great a fool.

11:43.230 --> 11:45.300
Well, I warned you.

12:16.210 --> 12:18.080
All right! Careful, now!

12:18.830 --> 12:21.380
All right! Everyone take a break!

12:19.170 --> 12:20.220
Raise it up!

12:29.800 --> 12:30.700
Want a drink?

12:32.170 --> 12:35.230
Are you all right? You look tired, but...

12:35.530 --> 12:36.920
Thank you.

12:36.920 --> 12:39.040
I do seem to be a little exhausted.

12:39.040 --> 12:41.660
It's because I finished my piece last night.

12:41.660 --> 12:43.660
Did you? Really?

12:43.660 --> 12:44.440
Yes.

12:44.440 --> 12:47.000
I'm so glad! You finished in time, then.

12:47.000 --> 12:49.420
The Sugar Confectionary Exhibition is 
the day after tomorrow.

12:49.420 --> 12:51.500
The truth is, I was a little worried for you.

12:51.920 --> 12:54.710
You've completed your piece, Halford?

12:56.090 --> 12:56.670
Yes, sir.

12:56.670 --> 13:00.190
Then, in accordance with the regulations, 
I will conduct an inspection.

13:00.190 --> 13:01.100
Any objections?

13:03.210 --> 13:04.380
Please, if you would.

13:04.940 --> 13:07.050
May I come along, too?

13:07.050 --> 13:09.180
I would very much like to see Anne's work.

13:09.180 --> 13:11.060
That won't pose a problem. Come.

13:15.140 --> 13:16.600
What are you doing?

13:16.600 --> 13:18.220
Mithril Lid Pod?

13:18.220 --> 13:20.060
N-Nothing.

13:20.060 --> 13:20.910
Where's Challe?

13:20.910 --> 13:23.050
Oh. I took proper measures 
to get him out of the—

13:23.050 --> 13:25.820
Uh, he's on a walk! A walk! Yup!

13:25.820 --> 13:28.350
Could it be... that you're sneaking a taste?

13:28.350 --> 13:29.200
N-No!

13:29.200 --> 13:30.910
I'm testing it! Taste testing!

13:30.910 --> 13:34.270
Anne, your silver sugar is 
exceptionally beautiful and silky...

13:34.270 --> 13:35.680
and it tastes different, too!

13:35.680 --> 13:37.500
It's light and delicious...

13:37.500 --> 13:39.980
Isn't that what people call 
"sneaking a taste"?

13:39.980 --> 13:43.980
Wait. Mithril Lid Pod, you can tell 
the differences in the silver sugar?

13:43.980 --> 13:45.380
All fairies can.

13:45.380 --> 13:46.560
Don't underestimate us!

13:46.560 --> 13:49.890
We didn't come to witness an argument 
between a human and a fairy.

13:50.200 --> 13:51.850
Oh, I-I'm so sorry!

14:04.660 --> 14:07.540
The climbing rose is a flower 
that symbolizes the royal family.

14:08.060 --> 14:11.110
You've taken that...
and used a fairy's wing to...

14:14.900 --> 14:17.210
Is... Is it all right?

14:17.960 --> 14:19.290
Y-Yes.

14:19.630 --> 14:21.790
It will do. It's rather impressive.

14:22.270 --> 14:23.750
Thank you!

14:29.280 --> 14:30.260
It's wonderful.

14:30.670 --> 14:31.360
What?

14:31.360 --> 14:33.840
Your piece. It's really wonderful.

14:33.840 --> 14:36.120
Really? Thank you!

14:36.640 --> 14:38.980
I have confidence in my skills.

14:39.520 --> 14:42.140
But after seeing your piece, Anne...

14:42.140 --> 14:44.310
I'm not sure why, but I feel uneasy.

14:45.010 --> 14:48.920
At any rate, I'm glad that I get to compete 
against you in the Exhibition.

14:48.920 --> 14:53.060
Let's stand before the king, in a place of fair 
impartiality, and ask for his majesty's judgment.

14:53.450 --> 14:54.370
It's a real contest!

14:54.650 --> 14:55.460
Yes!

14:58.740 --> 15:00.500
Why are you grinning like that?

15:00.840 --> 15:02.670
What has made you so happy?

15:02.670 --> 15:05.610
Kieth complimented my sugar confection!

15:05.610 --> 15:07.590
Being praised by someone so skilled...

15:07.590 --> 15:09.290
of course I'm happy!

15:18.080 --> 15:20.520
Jonas, do you need something?

15:20.520 --> 15:22.990
If I didn't, I wouldn't come here, would I?

15:22.990 --> 15:24.840
I ran into Sammy.

15:24.840 --> 15:27.880
He said that my uncle is looking for you, 
so you should go to the workrooms.

15:27.880 --> 15:29.480
Mister Radcliffe is?

15:29.480 --> 15:30.880
I wonder why.

15:30.880 --> 15:32.450
I'm going out for a minute!

15:36.970 --> 15:40.260
Uncle! I've brought Anne Halford!

15:47.400 --> 15:49.220
Thanks for that.

15:49.870 --> 15:52.680
But Mister Radcliffe isn't here.

15:59.390 --> 16:01.310
Sammy, what is this?

16:02.580 --> 16:05.560
Jonas, don't you find it frustrating?

16:05.560 --> 16:08.910
At the Sugar Confectionary Exhibition 
the day after tomorrow,

16:08.910 --> 16:11.400
this girl's gonna cheat 
her way to a royal medal.

16:11.900 --> 16:13.760
Last year, it was you.

16:13.760 --> 16:15.120
This year...

16:18.580 --> 16:21.740
you're humiliating Kieth!

16:21.740 --> 16:23.770
Wh-What are you talking about?

16:23.770 --> 16:25.120
When have I ever done that to Kieth?

16:25.120 --> 16:26.710
After seeing your work,

16:27.020 --> 16:29.210
Kieth said he felt uneasy!

16:29.210 --> 16:30.590
Because of those climbing roses!

16:31.080 --> 16:32.520
These hands...

16:32.520 --> 16:34.480
If these hands didn't exist...

16:33.810 --> 16:34.730
Please, don't!

16:34.480 --> 16:36.090
Sammy, this is going too far!

16:36.090 --> 16:39.580
I mean, I hate Anne, too, but this is just—

16:39.580 --> 16:42.970
If you're a member of the Radcliffe school, 
then watch to the very end!

16:42.970 --> 16:43.710
Ow!

16:43.710 --> 16:44.860
Master Jonas!

16:47.080 --> 16:49.230
Jonas! Get back here!

16:53.310 --> 16:56.080
Hey, Challe fenn Challe. Give me an answer.

16:56.080 --> 16:57.480
I'm going to ask a serious question.

16:58.160 --> 16:59.210
What is it?

16:59.800 --> 17:03.980
If a girl tells you she loves you 
and asks you to kiss you,

17:03.980 --> 17:05.960
are you the type that would enjoy that?

17:07.080 --> 17:10.520
From this point forward, 
I will not listen to your serious questions.

17:14.350 --> 17:15.550
A-Anne is...

17:17.240 --> 17:18.470
Stop!

17:18.470 --> 17:20.180
No!

17:24.380 --> 17:25.020
Anne is...

17:25.440 --> 17:26.350
Anne is...!

17:37.810 --> 17:38.990
Challe?

17:48.000 --> 17:50.750
You humans!

17:50.750 --> 17:52.600
No! Please, don't kill them!

17:58.490 --> 18:02.380
One day... I will kill you all.

18:02.380 --> 18:04.430
Just wait. I will not fail.

18:04.920 --> 18:05.910
I <i>will</i> kill you.

18:14.310 --> 18:15.110
Challe...

18:17.750 --> 18:18.980
I wasn't here.

18:23.000 --> 18:26.620
I let myself be separated from you.

18:29.510 --> 18:32.250
Challe, I was so scared.

18:33.360 --> 18:35.130
I was so scared.

18:41.530 --> 18:43.620
You're all right now.

18:55.190 --> 18:57.180
I heard what happened.

18:57.180 --> 19:00.890
As the master of the Radcliffe Workshop school, 
I offer you my deepest apologies.

19:01.620 --> 19:03.000
I am so sorry.

19:03.940 --> 19:06.160
What a horrible thing to happen.

19:06.460 --> 19:09.140
Truly, it brings shame upon our whole school.

19:11.400 --> 19:13.670
He's my nephew, but I've 
run out of patience with him.

19:14.190 --> 19:15.040
What?

19:17.590 --> 19:20.800
Jonas will be expelled 
from the Radcliffe school!

19:21.080 --> 19:22.910
Please, wait, Mister Radcliffe!

19:22.910 --> 19:24.800
It wasn't Jonas who did this!

19:25.260 --> 19:29.020
Then who was it that tried to hurt you?

19:29.510 --> 19:32.600
It was Sammy. Jonas was the one 
who got help for me.

19:33.860 --> 19:36.360
It was Sammy and the others 
who made the report!

19:36.700 --> 19:39.280
That is what brought me here.

19:39.280 --> 19:40.780
Sammy did that?

19:41.130 --> 19:44.190
Who would make a report of their own crimes?

19:44.190 --> 19:46.510
You have been treated horribly,

19:46.510 --> 19:48.360
but there are limits to 
what is acceptable to say.

19:48.360 --> 19:49.400
But!

19:49.400 --> 19:52.270
Sammy has worked for this workshop 
since the age of twelve.

19:52.270 --> 19:53.980
He was practically born an artisan.

19:53.980 --> 19:55.590
And he is one of my favorite apprentices.

19:56.390 --> 19:58.400
He would never lie to me!

19:58.400 --> 19:59.930
But he is, isn't he?

19:59.930 --> 20:02.800
Jonas showed up here on an errand first!

20:02.800 --> 20:05.760
He said that Sammy said you wanted her 
to come to the workrooms!

20:06.120 --> 20:07.680
Does that sound familiar?

20:07.680 --> 20:09.230
Make the fairy be quiet.

20:09.230 --> 20:11.980
After that, Jonas showed up 
looking like he was about to cry and—

20:11.180 --> 20:11.980
Make him be quiet!

20:11.980 --> 20:13.060
I won't be quiet!

20:13.360 --> 20:14.270
You little...

20:14.270 --> 20:15.310
Mithril!

20:19.860 --> 20:20.990
Challe.

20:21.640 --> 20:24.700
The fairy who served 
as the model for Kieth's piece.

20:24.700 --> 20:26.860
It was also you who saved Halford, wasn't it?

20:26.860 --> 20:28.360
Then I'll ask you.

20:28.360 --> 20:29.910
Who did this?

20:30.610 --> 20:34.380
Rotten apprentices only come 
from rotten masters.

20:38.580 --> 20:39.920
Get out.

20:40.280 --> 20:43.080
You and Jonas, all of you, get out.

20:43.080 --> 20:47.880
Take the three barrels of silver sugar you 
refined and the piece you made with you.

20:47.880 --> 20:51.430
It's the least the Radcliffe workshop can do 
to compensate you for the inconvenience.

20:52.530 --> 20:54.140
But, Mister Radcliffe, that's—

20:54.140 --> 20:55.020
Get out!

20:59.250 --> 21:04.990
That Which Should Be Made

21:16.250 --> 21:20.580
<i>Is it just like the dreams we dream at night?</i>

21:21.450 --> 21:26.720
<i>Do we give names to our other dreams because,</i>

21:26.720 --> 21:30.260
<i>Just as our night dreams 
are forgotten upon waking,</i>

21:30.260 --> 21:37.330
<i>If they aren't held dear, 
they will disappear?</i>

21:37.330 --> 21:48.470
<i>No, it's because they aren't things 
that only special people can see</i>

21:48.470 --> 21:49.200
<i>That day</i>

21:49.200 --> 21:53.650
<i>I reached out again and again</i>

21:53.650 --> 21:59.210
<i>I failed to catch that shining fruit, and yet</i>

21:59.210 --> 22:04.710
<i>I'll reach out once more</i>

22:04.710 --> 22:09.010
<i>If I make my wishes come true myself</i>

22:09.010 --> 22:14.840
<i>I just know it will make you smile</i>

22:14.840 --> 22:26.320
<i>That's why I'm able to say I'm not giving up</i>

22:36.140 --> 22:40.040
<b>I Didn't Want to Let Go</b>
